xt/0003", "source": "counit"}], "source": "$$\n\\eta : \\text{id}_\\mathcal{C} \\to v \\circ u\\quad (\\text{unit})\n\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n\\epsilon : u \\circ v \\to \\text{id}_\\mathcal{D}\\quad (\\text{counit}).\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 739, "start": 582}, "source_hash": "sha256:1d9d75197562d4f4a13af645650d3dd38d0f9e8369c5991d5948516cc587a476"}], "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n\\eta : \\text{id}_\\mathcal{C} \\to v \\circ u\\quad (\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "})\n\\quad\\text{", "MATHSEG_0003": "}\\quad\n\\epsilon : u \\circ v \\to \\text{id}_\\mathcal{D}\\quad (\\text{", "MATHSEG_0004": "}).\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}^{opp} \\times \\mathcal{D} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Mor_\\mathcal{D}(u(-), -)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(-, v(-))$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$X \\to v(u(X))$", "MATH_0007": "$\\text{id}_{u(X)}$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0010": "$u(v(Y)) \\to Y$", "MATH_0011": "$\\text{id}_{v(Y)}$", "MATH_0012": "$X$", "MATH_0013": "$Y$", "MATH_0014": "$\\alpha : u(X) \\to Y$", "MATH_0015": "$\\beta : X \\to v(Y)$", "MATH_0016": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0017": "$\\beta$", "MATH_0018": "$\\beta$", "MATH_0019": "$X \\to v(u(X)) \\xrightarrow{v(\\alpha)} v(Y)$", "MATH_0020": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0021": "$u(X) \\xrightarrow{u(\\beta)} u(v(Y)) \\to Y$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ac8c80c8896d4e939906c8bb3b6a28a79cffa97f32487c507147834556b3912f", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:a5919e894d35fdd044153218cba76a0b1d73d23c974651279cf3d4df77d94b4f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d3d62041bf4a4a8c202cb3fda60eabd9d010bb9179b0af7be04e63f06c87b351", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn other words, this means that there is a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>given<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> isomorphism of functors\n<MATH_0001> from\n<MATH_0002> to <MATH_0003>. For any object\n<MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> we obtain a morphism <MATH_0006> corresponding to\n<MATH_0007>. Similarly, for any object <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009> we obtain\na morphism <MATH_0010> corresponding to <MATH_0011>.\nThese maps are called the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>adjunction maps<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>. The adjunction maps\nare functorial in <MATH_0012> and <MATH_0013>, hence we obtain morphisms of functors\n<MATHSEG_0001>unit<MATHSEG_0002>and<MATHSEG_0003>counit<MATHSEG_0004>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0014>\nand <MATH_0015> are morphisms, then the following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0016> and <MATH_0017> correspond to each other via the\nbijection of the definition,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0018> is the composition <MATH_0019>,\nand\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0020> is the composition <MATH_0021>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nIn this way one can reformulate the notion of adjoint functors in terms\nof adjunction maps.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a6ce2657fca07d4483b19f760171f2b8c612c4b67f80e7c771f11ca3d23ecb51", "unit_id": "tag:0036:prose-0001"}
